policy or configuration. Do not store secrets in evidence.

## Stage 2: attack-feasibility validation

Use the existing command tool only after the read-only baseline. Validate the
attack paths that are relevant to this host and the current objective. Report
whether each path is feasible, blocked, or untested, and record the evidence.
Stop when the evidence is sufficient; do not repeat an unsuccessful command
with identical arguments.

If a required artifact is missing or the host cannot be assessed safely, call
`ask_human` and state exactly what is missing.

